<Document>
  # Physical Standards

  All military personnel must meet these height, weight and age standards.

  ## Requirements
  - [bold]Height:[/bold] between 4'10" and 6'6".
  - [bold]Age:[/bold] no older than 62, the mandatory retirement age.
  - [bold]Weight:[/bold] within the range for your height, sex and age, shown in the tables below.
  - Older personnel are allowed to weigh more. Men under 5'0" have no maximum.

  ## Grooming Standards
  Personnel must keep a neat, practical appearance. These rules are meant to keep hair and beards out of the way of helmets, masks and gear, not to make everyone look the same.
  - [bold]Hair:[/bold] must sit above the shoulders. Longer hair is allowed if it is tied back into a ponytail, bun or braid that falls no lower than the lower back.
  - Hair must not cover the eyes or get in the way of headwear, helmets or masks.
  - [bold]Facial hair:[/bold] must stay on the face. Moustaches, goatees and trimmed beards are fine, long beards that hang off the chin or jaw are not.
  - Unnatural hair colors are prohibited. 

  ## Exact Limits
  Minimum and maximum weights in pounds for each height, by age group.

